data.content:
## .NET 10 OpenAPI Breaking Changes

The root cause is **Microsoft.OpenApi upgraded from v1 → v2**, which redesigned the object model. Here are the four breaks and their fixes:

### 1. `OpenApiString` / `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` removed
The `IOpenApiAny` type hierarchy is gone. Use `System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonNode` instead:

```csharp
// Before
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;
param.Schema.Example = new OpenApiString("1.0");

// After
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
```

### 2. `OpenApiReference` + `ReferenceType` replaced by reference model types
Instead of creating a model and setting its `Reference` property, use the dedicated reference class from `Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References`:

```csharp
// Before
var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
{
    Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
};

// After
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References;
var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2");
```

### 3. `schema.Nullable` removed
OpenAPI 3.1 (which v2 targets) expresses nullability via the `type` keyword. The `Nullable` property is gone; manipulate the `JsonSchemaType` flags enum instead:

```csharp
// Before
property.Value.Nullable = false;

// After
property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
```

### 4. Full corrected code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2");
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

**Summary of namespace changes:**
| Removed | Replacement |
|---|---|
| `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` (`OpenApiString`, etc.) | `System.Text.Json.Nodes` (`JsonValue.Create(...)`) |
| `OpenApiReference` + `ReferenceType` enum | `Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References.*Reference` classes |
| `OpenApiSchema.Nullable` (bool) | `OpenApiSchema.Type` (`JsonSchemaType` flags, remove `Null` flag) |
